##DESCRIPTION
## frequency and period
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Mechanics)
## DBchapter(Oscillations)
## DBsection(Period and Frequency in Oscillatons)
## Date(26 December 2017)
## Institution(Brock University)
## Author(Santo D'Agostino)
## TitleText('')
## AuthorText('')
## EditionText('2018')
## Section('16.2')
## Problem('12')
## KEYWORDS(frequency, period, kinematics)

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'randomPerson.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric');

$a = random(8, 10, 0.5);
$b = random(4, 6,  0.2);
$T = 2 * $a / $b;
$f = 1 / $T;
$p = randomPerson();

BEGIN_PGML
During a training exercise, [$p] runs back and forth between two spots that are [`[$a]`] m apart. She keeps up a constant speed of [`[$b]`] m/s, and we can assume that the time she takes to turn at the endpoints of her motion is negligible.

a) Determine the period of [$p]'s motion.

    [_]{$T} [`\textrm{s}`]

b) Determine the frequency of [$p->their] motion.

    [_]{$f} [`\textrm{Hz}`]

END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();